WEBVTT

00:01:07.650 --> 00:01:08.650
It's me!

00:01:09.250 --> 00:01:11.130
Make up, make up, make up. It's me.

00:01:11.850 --> 00:01:13.610
Nobody there, okay? It's just a panic
attack.

00:01:27.580 --> 00:01:28.580
Come here.

00:01:29.820 --> 00:01:31.960
No, no, no, I can't. No, no, no, no.

00:01:32.380 --> 00:01:34.260
Now, Amy. You have to go now.

00:02:46.529 --> 00:02:47.590
It's the middle of the night.

00:03:23.060 --> 00:03:24.060
Morning, Miss Watson.

00:03:40.180 --> 00:03:41.180
Coming?

00:03:41.960 --> 00:03:48.920
You know, statistically, you are much

00:03:48.920 --> 00:03:51.620
more likely to die in a plane crash than
you are in a lift.

00:03:52.320 --> 00:03:55.120
But seeing as you're scared of heights,
I guess we won't be getting you on a

00:03:55.120 --> 00:03:56.320
plane anytime soon.

00:03:56.540 --> 00:03:57.540
Come on.

00:03:57.980 --> 00:03:58.980
To the stairs.

00:04:00.440 --> 00:04:02.020
We're saving a fortune on gym fees.

00:05:08.010 --> 00:05:10.930
That's the contract you signed the day
you came to work here.

00:05:11.970 --> 00:05:16.450
Now, it clearly states that you will
disclose the results of all tests run by

00:05:16.450 --> 00:05:18.270
you or any of your subordinates.

00:05:19.930 --> 00:05:23.530
As part of Amy's condition. I know what
her condition is.

00:05:24.810 --> 00:05:28.510
But we happen to be stood in one of the
most advanced buildings ever constructed

00:05:28.510 --> 00:05:34.350
when the thing that Miss Watson claimed
to have isn't actually recognised by a

00:05:34.350 --> 00:05:37.630
single... medical organization anywhere
in the world.

00:05:39.050 --> 00:05:43.190
And this condition should not preclude
her from handing over that information.

00:05:45.770 --> 00:05:51.490
Now, this company has invested tens of
millions in you. We built shielding

00:05:51.490 --> 00:05:55.490
materials and anti-frequency film into
the walls of this laboratory. There are

00:05:55.490 --> 00:05:59.630
grounding mats under the floor. We gave
you a bunch of millions to work the

00:05:59.630 --> 00:06:01.450
equipment for you and clean up after
you.

00:06:02.090 --> 00:06:04.250
And what I can't understand is why you
refuse.

00:06:05.610 --> 00:06:06.930
This is your life's work.

00:06:07.190 --> 00:06:11.230
To save the world from a disease that
took your own mother's life.

00:06:12.870 --> 00:06:16.310
It goes onto a computer. Do you
understand?

00:06:53.230 --> 00:06:55.390
You know everything has to go on to the
system.

00:06:57.070 --> 00:06:58.730
It's the only way to secure it.

00:06:59.510 --> 00:07:03.170
And to prove or disprove any theory you
may have.

00:07:05.490 --> 00:07:09.030
You've already received two written
warnings. I suggest you don't make it a

00:07:09.030 --> 00:07:10.030
third.

00:07:17.570 --> 00:07:20.290
This company has shown considerable
faith in you.

00:07:21.190 --> 00:07:24.590
Alongside. billions of dollars for
shareholders' money.

00:07:26.610 --> 00:07:29.990
Might you want to explore the
possibility that the needle you're

00:07:29.990 --> 00:07:31.530
looking for no longer exists?

00:08:07.130 --> 00:08:09.610
I'm in bed when you leave, and in bed
when you get home.

00:08:10.390 --> 00:08:12.150
If you didn't wake me, we'd never see
each other.

00:08:13.090 --> 00:08:14.790
I think I'm wasting their money.

00:08:20.750 --> 00:08:22.170
Tell me about the mountains.

00:08:24.070 --> 00:08:25.350
You've heard it a hundred times.

00:08:28.050 --> 00:08:29.410
It's like being on top of the world.

00:08:33.730 --> 00:08:34.730
Take me there.

00:08:35.409 --> 00:08:36.409
To the mountains?

00:08:37.520 --> 00:08:38.820
You can't ride an elevator.

00:08:42.340 --> 00:08:45.060
Do you ever think about finding someone
else?

00:08:46.820 --> 00:08:48.880
Someone you can do all these things
with?

00:08:49.860 --> 00:08:50.860
All the time.

00:08:51.880 --> 00:08:55.980
But you know how hard it is to find a
monumentally stubborn, sexy, genius

00:08:55.980 --> 00:08:56.980
girlfriend, Ella?

00:09:37.200 --> 00:09:38.200
You know what this means?

00:09:39.020 --> 00:09:41.880
If you can match the pathogens, this
could change everything.

00:09:43.120 --> 00:09:44.120
Write it up.

00:09:44.440 --> 00:09:46.520
Everything must go onto the system.

00:09:46.940 --> 00:09:49.460
I'll inform the board. The directors
will want to know.

00:09:51.120 --> 00:09:52.120
Good work.

00:10:45.390 --> 00:10:48.890
Okay, guys, let's make a move, please.
Day one. Thank you.

00:11:16.400 --> 00:11:17.400
Did you know?

00:11:19.880 --> 00:11:21.480
Did you know they were going to fire us?

00:11:23.700 --> 00:11:24.700
So you did know.

00:11:27.940 --> 00:11:31.080
Because of your research, they're moving
resources onto clinical trials.

00:11:33.700 --> 00:11:35.000
They said we're no longer needed.

00:11:41.120 --> 00:11:42.600
Do you not have anything to say?

00:11:45.550 --> 00:11:51.530
No, it's just... I thought that we were
in this together.

00:11:58.530 --> 00:12:03.150
You know, I've spent ten years
microwaving your samples because you

00:12:03.150 --> 00:12:04.150
can't use the machines.

00:12:05.090 --> 00:12:09.930
I have washed thousands of Petri dishes
and slides, and I have walked you up

00:12:09.930 --> 00:12:13.050
these stairs every single day because
you can't get in a lift by yourself.

00:12:14.010 --> 00:12:15.490
And you can't even look at me.

00:12:20.850 --> 00:12:22.330
There was nothing I could do.

00:12:28.750 --> 00:12:31.590
Do you think any of the people in this
building care about you?

00:12:32.130 --> 00:12:36.110
Because they will use you up until there
is nothing left and they will throw you

00:12:36.110 --> 00:12:37.290
away like the rest of us!

00:12:48.390 --> 00:12:49.690
See? What did I tell you?

00:12:50.330 --> 00:12:51.330
Still alive.

00:12:53.010 --> 00:12:54.330
Now all you need to do is switch on.

00:13:06.970 --> 00:13:13.370
Can you just stay home today?

00:13:15.070 --> 00:13:16.410
I have to show my face at work.

00:13:17.620 --> 00:13:18.660
I'll be back in a few hours.

00:13:49.170 --> 00:13:51.810
Hey, I've got a couple of miles down the
road in Fort Washington. Let's spend the

00:13:51.810 --> 00:13:52.810
day with my girl.

00:15:16.370 --> 00:15:18.570
Robert got these for me.

00:15:22.510 --> 00:15:26.610
I made him promise to take me to these
mountains.

00:15:29.810 --> 00:15:34.030
And now I want you to take him there.

00:15:38.090 --> 00:15:40.510
No, Robert bought these tickets for you.

00:15:41.830 --> 00:15:43.450
He wanted you to see it.

00:15:49.420 --> 00:15:50.420
You can't.

00:15:50.520 --> 00:15:54.020
Amy, you spent your whole life proving
people wrong.

00:15:55.100 --> 00:15:59.900
I mean, those pricks tried to tell you
that your research wouldn't work. And

00:15:59.900 --> 00:16:00.900
what happened?

00:16:00.940 --> 00:16:02.160
You made it work.

00:16:03.560 --> 00:16:08.140
And Robert, he believed in you.

00:16:09.600 --> 00:16:11.360
That's why he bought you these tickets.

00:16:11.880 --> 00:16:13.300
Because he knew you could do it.

00:16:14.600 --> 00:16:15.680
With him, maybe.

00:16:21.079 --> 00:16:22.220
Well, what if I weren't with you?

00:16:34.440 --> 00:16:37.040
I don't know if you might recognize the
place. Have you seen it before?

00:16:38.140 --> 00:16:39.540
Would you be able to walk around?

00:16:39.880 --> 00:16:42.700
Yeah, sure. Thank you so much. Have a
nice day.

00:16:49.260 --> 00:16:50.260
He doesn't know the place.

00:16:51.470 --> 00:16:52.470
It's okay, though.

00:16:52.670 --> 00:16:53.670
We'll find it.

00:16:59.570 --> 00:17:04.890
Nobody knows up here, so we could be
whoever we wanted to be.

00:17:06.050 --> 00:17:09.390
I think that I will be Karina.

00:17:09.910 --> 00:17:13.369
I am a filmmaker scouting locations for
the next project.

00:17:13.790 --> 00:17:17.630
And who would you be? You would be
Joanna. No, Alex.

00:17:18.270 --> 00:17:21.990
You are a party planner. You are an
event manager for the stars.

00:17:23.450 --> 00:17:24.450
Yeah.

00:17:24.569 --> 00:17:25.829
Yeah, there she is.

00:17:26.550 --> 00:17:29.550
That's Alex. Hey, I asked around and I
know a guy who knows your shrine.

00:17:30.050 --> 00:17:33.230
A few of us are going for a climb, so I
was thinking we could all go together if

00:17:33.230 --> 00:17:34.230
you like.

00:17:35.510 --> 00:17:36.570
I'm Bart, by the way.

00:17:36.770 --> 00:17:38.290
Karina and Alex.

00:17:41.410 --> 00:17:42.470
Sorry, I forgot.

00:17:43.090 --> 00:17:44.090
Kat.

00:17:45.590 --> 00:17:47.370
Evan. Yeah, Evan knows your place.

00:17:48.000 --> 00:17:51.160
It's one of the most beautiful places
I've ever seen.

00:17:51.700 --> 00:17:52.920
Yeah. Shall we?

00:17:53.740 --> 00:17:54.740
Let's do it.

00:18:43.350 --> 00:18:47.410
I don't think you're supposed to be
doing that. Oh, a fat lot of difference

00:18:47.410 --> 00:18:48.610
that's going to make now.

00:18:50.450 --> 00:18:56.330
They say we shouldn't use words like
terminal and dying around here because

00:18:56.330 --> 00:18:59.850
it doesn't promote a positive mental
attitude.

00:19:02.330 --> 00:19:03.330
It's all here.

00:19:04.350 --> 00:19:05.790
Everything you asked me for.

00:19:08.270 --> 00:19:09.850
What it feels like to be dying.

00:19:10.930 --> 00:19:12.270
Each one from the inside.

00:19:16.110 --> 00:19:17.110
Listen to me.

00:19:18.090 --> 00:19:19.090
What you have.

00:19:19.790 --> 00:19:21.790
Your OCD. Most people.

00:19:23.070 --> 00:19:24.330
They think that's sickness.

00:19:25.730 --> 00:19:27.970
They're going to call you a freak. But.

00:19:30.010 --> 00:19:32.630
It's the obsession and the compulsion
part.

00:19:32.910 --> 00:19:36.510
The attention to detail. That is a
thing.

00:19:37.320 --> 00:19:43.100
They will keep you going when everybody
else has already given up. So you... You

00:19:43.100 --> 00:19:44.260
must embrace that.

00:19:48.960 --> 00:19:49.960
That book.

00:19:51.480 --> 00:19:52.960
All it needs is an ending.

00:19:55.160 --> 00:19:56.160
Not my girl.

00:19:56.840 --> 00:19:57.840
That's up to you.

00:20:03.720 --> 00:20:04.720
Hey.

00:20:06.800 --> 00:20:08.320
You've got this, alright?

00:20:09.420 --> 00:20:11.700
Forget about the lab and all of those
fucknuggets.

00:20:12.680 --> 00:20:13.680
Look at this place.

00:20:14.420 --> 00:20:16.080
This is what Robert wanted you to see.

00:20:59.229 --> 00:21:00.950
So, what brings you guys out here?

00:21:02.350 --> 00:21:06.270
I'm considering the area for a film that
I'm working on. Oh, right.

00:21:08.030 --> 00:21:09.030
What about you?

00:21:09.970 --> 00:21:11.810
You out here working on a movie as well?

00:21:13.590 --> 00:21:18.710
No, it's... It's more a face-my-fears
situation.

00:21:19.290 --> 00:21:20.330
You've got a lot of them, have you?

00:21:21.910 --> 00:21:22.910
Yeah.

00:21:23.430 --> 00:21:24.430
Mine's spiders.

00:21:25.090 --> 00:21:27.070
Eight legs, eight eyes.

00:21:27.680 --> 00:21:30.080
Now what's all that about? How well do
you need to see that you've got to have

00:21:30.080 --> 00:21:31.080
eight eyes?

00:22:00.680 --> 00:22:02.960
I think this is a good spot for a break.

00:22:14.580 --> 00:22:16.160
The old zipline anchor point.

00:22:16.660 --> 00:22:20.340
They put them here in World War I to
move ammunition and supplies instead of

00:22:20.340 --> 00:22:21.340
humping them across the valley.

00:22:22.380 --> 00:22:27.080
They also say the secret spies used them
to send messages from one town to the

00:22:27.080 --> 00:22:28.080
other.

00:22:30.250 --> 00:22:31.870
Most of the lines are in disrepair.

00:22:32.830 --> 00:22:34.230
Even loose and slack over time.

00:22:35.330 --> 00:22:36.330
Broken completely.

00:22:37.750 --> 00:22:39.310
But there are still a few in use.

00:22:41.290 --> 00:22:43.770
I mean, they still use them to move
livestock down the mountain.

00:22:44.610 --> 00:22:46.310
So, who's first?

00:22:48.110 --> 00:22:50.070
Come on, they've been here for a hundred
years.

00:22:51.550 --> 00:22:52.550
What, nobody?

00:22:52.790 --> 00:22:53.790
Where's your sense of adventure?

00:22:55.790 --> 00:22:56.790
Okay, fine.

00:22:57.640 --> 00:23:00.260
I guess if you don't want to go up this
one, there's no point taking up the Big

00:23:00.260 --> 00:23:01.260
Blue.

00:23:01.320 --> 00:23:02.320
The Big Blue?

00:23:03.200 --> 00:23:05.240
The mother of all the zip wires.

00:23:06.600 --> 00:23:10.320
They saw these old ones and thought of a
way of exploiting sloppy tourists.

00:23:11.180 --> 00:23:14.360
There's one in South Africa called K3,
about two miles long.

00:23:14.900 --> 00:23:18.380
But once it's finished, the Big Blue
makes it look like something you can

00:23:18.380 --> 00:23:19.380
hang your washing on.

00:23:22.980 --> 00:23:23.980
Shall we?

00:23:45.879 --> 00:23:46.879
New boot?

00:23:46.920 --> 00:23:47.920
Yeah.

00:23:48.240 --> 00:23:52.860
All right. Come sit down. Let me take a
look. No. Seriously, if you've got new

00:23:52.860 --> 00:23:54.200
boots, let me take a look.

00:23:55.300 --> 00:23:56.300
New boots.

00:23:56.560 --> 00:23:57.560
Lucky mistake.

00:24:02.080 --> 00:24:03.480
Take it off. Let me have a look.

00:24:03.780 --> 00:24:05.540
Boots need to be worn in before you get
out of here.

00:24:08.520 --> 00:24:09.780
Ooh, how does that look sore?

00:24:10.100 --> 00:24:11.920
All right, no shrine for you today.

00:24:14.220 --> 00:24:15.880
Oh, aren't you a little Florence
Nightingale?

00:24:16.160 --> 00:24:17.160
Boy scout.

00:24:17.380 --> 00:24:18.380
Right.

00:24:18.680 --> 00:24:21.440
Listen, this is going to take me a few
minutes. Why don't you guys carry on and

00:24:21.440 --> 00:24:24.220
take a look at the zip wire? It's just
around that ledge on for another 20

00:24:24.220 --> 00:24:25.220
minutes.

00:24:26.380 --> 00:24:28.780
Seriously, there's no point in coming
all this way and not seeing it.

00:24:29.020 --> 00:24:30.020
No?

00:24:30.080 --> 00:24:31.080
Yeah.

00:24:32.419 --> 00:24:33.580
Okay, just do it.

00:24:34.540 --> 00:24:35.540
Okay.

00:24:36.140 --> 00:24:37.140
I'll see you soon.

00:24:39.500 --> 00:24:40.500
Okay, ready?

00:24:41.140 --> 00:24:42.460
Just gonna clean it, alright?

00:24:43.640 --> 00:24:44.640
Alright.

00:24:44.880 --> 00:24:45.880
There you go.

00:25:08.400 --> 00:25:09.400
There's no sign of them.

00:25:10.140 --> 00:25:11.140
Weird.

00:25:11.240 --> 00:25:12.720
It's been like two hours now.

00:25:14.100 --> 00:25:19.420
I don't know them, so I don't have their
numbers. Can you give your friend a

00:25:19.420 --> 00:25:20.299
call?

00:25:20.300 --> 00:25:21.300
I don't have a phone.

00:25:22.220 --> 00:25:23.300
You don't have a phone?

00:25:24.700 --> 00:25:27.000
Right. Living off grid for a few days.
Nice.

00:25:27.240 --> 00:25:28.340
Wish I could do the same.

00:25:28.940 --> 00:25:31.740
I've got bosses to answer to. They like
to keep me on a leash.

00:25:32.560 --> 00:25:33.560
All right.

00:25:33.880 --> 00:25:35.960
Does your friend have Facebook?

00:25:36.240 --> 00:25:37.260
Something like that.

00:25:38.380 --> 00:25:39.760
Do you think something's happened to
them?

00:25:40.620 --> 00:25:41.620
No, they'll be fine.

00:25:42.120 --> 00:25:43.900
The other two seem pretty experienced.

00:25:45.600 --> 00:25:48.620
With your foot the way it is, it's a
really rough trek back the way we came,

00:25:48.680 --> 00:25:49.680
but I know a shortcut.

00:25:50.080 --> 00:25:53.320
It's a bit hairy in one spot, but it'll
save you a couple of hours walking.

00:25:53.860 --> 00:25:54.860
Yeah, shall we head back?

00:25:56.980 --> 00:25:57.980
Yeah.

00:26:04.800 --> 00:26:05.800
OK.

00:26:06.300 --> 00:26:07.660
Let's use this. You all right? Yeah.

00:26:08.270 --> 00:26:09.630
Put your hand on here for stability.

00:26:09.970 --> 00:26:10.970
Just use this.

00:26:11.790 --> 00:26:12.790
Okay?

00:26:13.930 --> 00:26:15.170
That's it. We're straight down there.

00:26:16.310 --> 00:26:17.310
Okay,

00:26:20.350 --> 00:26:27.650
I

00:26:27.650 --> 00:26:30.390
saw that. I am clipping you on. Just
stop, stop, stop.

00:26:31.330 --> 00:26:33.550
Make you feel a bit more secure. Put
your foot through here.

00:26:34.050 --> 00:26:35.050
That's it. There.

00:26:36.010 --> 00:26:37.010
All right.

00:26:37.110 --> 00:26:38.880
And then... Hold it up over your head.

00:26:39.540 --> 00:26:40.479
That's it.

00:26:40.480 --> 00:26:41.960
That will get you clipped in.

00:26:43.840 --> 00:26:45.400
I've got a carabiner here somewhere.

00:26:47.920 --> 00:26:50.420
I've got you now, okay? Just carry on
straight down there.

00:27:11.690 --> 00:27:12.690
It really is beautiful here.

00:27:21.510 --> 00:27:22.790
You okay, Alex?

00:27:24.850 --> 00:27:25.850
Huh?

00:27:26.970 --> 00:27:28.930
Or should I call you Amy?

00:27:35.550 --> 00:27:41.030
To my dearest Amy, winners are the
dreamers.

00:27:41.500 --> 00:27:42.500
Never give up.

00:27:44.300 --> 00:27:45.820
Love you always, Mum.

00:27:46.340 --> 00:27:48.560
It's nice. It's a bit cheesy, but it's
nice.

00:27:49.440 --> 00:27:54.740
As for the rest of what's in this book,
you know they had some top Palo Alto

00:27:54.740 --> 00:27:56.700
geeks try and crack this code of yours.

00:27:57.880 --> 00:27:59.660
Apparently it's genius level.

00:28:01.000 --> 00:28:03.120
Like you're some kind of savant or
something.

00:28:04.680 --> 00:28:08.160
Yeah, well, they tried their way.

00:28:09.960 --> 00:28:11.480
Now it's time to try mine.

00:28:14.920 --> 00:28:20.060
Amy, do you know what happens to the
human body when it hits the ground from

00:28:20.060 --> 00:28:21.060
a height like this?

00:28:22.000 --> 00:28:23.000
It's fascinating.

00:28:24.980 --> 00:28:26.480
It liquidizes.

00:28:27.300 --> 00:28:33.740
All those bones, internal organs, that
brilliant brain of yours just turns into

00:28:33.740 --> 00:28:34.920
a puddle of mush.

00:28:35.780 --> 00:28:37.500
Why don't you just give me the code?

00:28:48.750 --> 00:28:49.750
Well, just like that.

00:28:50.910 --> 00:28:52.730
Well, now you've got me thinking it's
too easy.

00:28:52.970 --> 00:28:53.970
Just pull me up.

00:28:54.190 --> 00:28:55.190
No, no, no.

00:28:55.490 --> 00:28:58.190
That's not how it's going to work. Not
with that big brain of yours. I don't

00:28:58.190 --> 00:28:59.190
know if I can take the risk.

00:29:02.950 --> 00:29:04.490
If I tell you, you'll let me fall.

00:29:05.450 --> 00:29:08.390
I guess we can add trust issues to the
list.

00:29:08.850 --> 00:29:11.690
Look, they paid me to get the code, not
to kill you.

00:29:12.210 --> 00:29:14.890
Anyway, you are not in a position to
negotiate, darling.

00:29:18.890 --> 00:29:20.990
How am I going to explain it to someone
like you?

00:29:22.770 --> 00:29:24.570
Did you just throw me shade?

