01:04:40.040 --> 01:04:42.160
I wanted you to know how it feels to not
matter.

01:04:45.640 --> 01:04:46.740
But I had no idea.

01:04:52.360 --> 01:04:53.360
I'm sorry.

01:04:54.320 --> 01:04:57.600
What's in that book won't matter if you
don't make it out of here.

01:05:03.320 --> 01:05:04.320
What are you doing?

01:05:05.660 --> 01:05:07.840
He's right. That's why I won't hold both
of us.

01:05:09.470 --> 01:05:11.070
No, no, Chloe, no.

01:05:13.010 --> 01:05:14.310
Think about your mum.

01:05:15.490 --> 01:05:17.230
Think about the people just like her.

01:05:18.710 --> 01:05:20.070
Your book can help them.

01:05:21.350 --> 01:05:22.350
Okay?

01:05:24.470 --> 01:05:29.930
No, no, Chloe, Chloe, you must be close.
No, you must, you must, you must, you

01:05:29.930 --> 01:05:32.790
must. I don't know. I'm not scared.

01:06:16.140 --> 01:06:17.140
That's what you want?

01:06:24.480 --> 01:06:26.800
We made copies of the book, Amy.

01:06:27.920 --> 01:06:29.380
All we need is the code.

01:06:38.900 --> 01:06:43.140
It's the obsession and the compulsion
part. That is the thing.

01:06:44.040 --> 01:06:46.820
They will keep you going when everybody
else has already given up.

01:07:16.970 --> 01:07:22.410
Days and the nights and the weekends and
the birthdays and the Christmases I've

01:07:22.410 --> 01:07:23.410
lost.

01:07:25.790 --> 01:07:27.150
Stuck in a room.

01:07:30.430 --> 01:07:36.810
My mom used to say this OCD

01:07:36.810 --> 01:07:41.030
called anxiety is what made me
different.

01:07:41.710 --> 01:07:43.490
It's what made me special.

01:09:25.870 --> 01:09:29.569
Real shame, Amy, if all this was for
nothing.

01:12:00.000 --> 01:12:01.000
Amen?

01:12:15.140 --> 01:12:16.140
Amen?

01:13:12.520 --> 01:13:13.800
You missed this, Amy.

01:13:14.800 --> 01:13:16.520
This lovely ice pick.

01:13:17.620 --> 01:13:19.360
Found it next to Chloe's body.

01:13:20.480 --> 01:13:21.560
Wasn't a pretty sight.

01:13:22.360 --> 01:13:24.600
I can see why your boyfriend liked it
here.

01:13:25.980 --> 01:13:26.980
Beautiful.

01:13:29.520 --> 01:13:32.600
You know, it wasn't supposed to be that
way that day in your apartment.

01:13:33.800 --> 01:13:35.800
You were supposed to be in the lab, Amy.

01:13:36.820 --> 01:13:38.740
You were supposed to be at work.

01:13:40.270 --> 01:13:44.050
Yeah, I guess I probably hit him a bit
hard. It's a shame.

01:13:45.770 --> 01:13:47.490
There's always collateral damage.

01:13:53.090 --> 01:13:54.250
That doesn't matter.

01:13:55.990 --> 01:13:58.790
What matters is what's in your book,
Amy.

01:14:00.150 --> 01:14:02.130
All those lives you can save.

01:14:03.350 --> 01:14:04.350
Amy?

01:15:16.170 --> 01:15:17.630
Let's go fishing.

01:18:38.740 --> 01:18:41.000
Well, I'm bad when you leave, and I'm
bad when you get home.

01:18:43.160 --> 01:18:44.960
If you didn't wake me, we'd never see
each other.

01:18:50.260 --> 01:18:54.540
But you know how hard it is to find a
monumentally stubborn, sexy, genius

01:18:54.540 --> 01:18:55.540
girlfriend, aren't you?

01:20:01.350 --> 01:20:02.510
Is it okay? Look at me.

01:20:02.790 --> 01:20:03.790
Are you okay?

01:20:07.530 --> 01:20:13.810
This is your statement.

01:20:14.970 --> 01:20:15.970
Is it okay?

01:20:19.830 --> 01:20:20.830
There was a call.

01:20:21.770 --> 01:20:23.210
Someone is coming here for you.

01:20:23.550 --> 01:20:24.610
A Donaldson.

01:20:26.390 --> 01:20:27.390
They're on their way.

01:20:33.320 --> 01:20:34.640
Do you know where this shrine is?

01:21:51.430 --> 01:21:55.030
The director sent me to bring you back.
Your research needs to be completed.

01:21:56.850 --> 01:21:58.550
You can come back to the lab, Amy.

01:22:02.610 --> 01:22:03.870
I don't have the book.

01:22:05.290 --> 01:22:06.830
What do you mean you don't have it?

01:22:08.630 --> 01:22:09.630
I hid it.

01:22:11.570 --> 01:22:12.570
I'll show you where.

01:22:13.690 --> 01:22:15.210
It's just further along here.

01:22:24.780 --> 01:22:25.960
They killed Robert.

01:22:27.240 --> 01:22:28.380
They're not a flat.

01:22:30.940 --> 01:22:33.860
Did you tell anyone the code? Anyone at
all?

01:22:46.160 --> 01:22:50.340
How did you know where to find me?

01:22:51.380 --> 01:22:53.700
I put a tracker in the phone I gave you.

01:22:54.920 --> 01:22:56.500
I'm sorry I should have told you.

01:23:04.800 --> 01:23:05.920
Of course.

01:23:06.720 --> 01:23:07.860
I was stupid.

01:23:09.780 --> 01:23:12.340
The phone, you didn't switch it on, did
you?

01:23:51.140 --> 01:23:52.140
Amy? Amy.

01:23:53.760 --> 01:23:56.540
I run a billion-pound company, Amy.

01:23:57.240 --> 01:24:00.240
Have you ever thought about the kind of
things I had to do to get there?

01:24:00.880 --> 01:24:01.880
Hmm?

01:24:03.120 --> 01:24:05.240
I never won a scholarship to Harvard.

01:24:05.840 --> 01:24:09.660
I wasn't top of my class and wanted by
every big farmer in the country.

01:24:11.040 --> 01:24:14.180
Huh? Nobody ever built me a special
laboratory.

01:24:15.650 --> 01:24:19.450
I never got married. I never had
children. I never even lived with anyone

01:24:19.450 --> 01:24:22.710
because there wasn't the time I was
running this company.

01:24:25.850 --> 01:24:27.790
And now you want to throw it all away?

01:24:29.810 --> 01:24:30.950
I'm not going to let you.

01:24:32.350 --> 01:24:33.790
I'm not going to let you do that.

01:24:35.690 --> 01:24:37.170
Get the fuck out here, Amy.

01:24:38.610 --> 01:24:39.610
It's a business.

01:24:40.330 --> 01:24:45.990
We sell pills to fund more research to
make more pills. It's a business of pain

01:24:45.990 --> 01:24:52.530
You

01:24:52.530 --> 01:25:04.790
want

01:25:04.790 --> 01:25:08.610
to bury my research I want to own it

01:25:11.310 --> 01:25:12.310
to be doctors.

01:25:13.350 --> 01:25:15.070
We're supposed to help people.

01:25:15.510 --> 01:25:16.510
Help them?

01:25:17.190 --> 01:25:18.550
They know what's killing them.

01:25:18.950 --> 01:25:21.030
Junk food, booze, ciggies.

01:25:21.470 --> 01:25:24.890
They need to get their fucking arses up
off the couch every now and then and

01:25:24.890 --> 01:25:28.010
move. But no, that's too hard for them,
thank goodness.

01:25:28.510 --> 01:25:33.170
We sell them a lifetime of pills, just
enough to keep them limping along.

01:25:34.170 --> 01:25:36.830
The last thing we want is a cure.

01:25:42.380 --> 01:25:43.480
You're going to give me the coat.

01:25:44.140 --> 01:25:47.200
You're going to give me the coat. I'm
going to put your face through this

01:25:47.200 --> 01:25:48.200
window.

01:25:50.040 --> 01:25:51.100
You've lost everything.

01:25:51.780 --> 01:25:56.540
You're a silly little girl who's lost
her mum who needs to grow up. Give me

01:25:56.540 --> 01:25:57.540
the coat.

01:26:01.000 --> 01:26:02.000
Too late.

01:26:28.619 --> 01:26:30.600
Amy, what did you do?

01:26:32.000 --> 01:26:35.960
You posted it all online You

01:26:35.960 --> 01:26:40.720
posted it all online

01:28:19.880 --> 01:28:25.040
A major medical breakthrough has emerged
under unusual circumstances as a formula

01:28:25.040 --> 01:28:28.440
believed to cure lung cancer has
reportedly been leaked online.

01:28:28.860 --> 01:28:33.220
Leading researchers say the treatment
could fundamentally change how cancer is

01:28:33.220 --> 01:28:36.460
approached. Authorities are now
investigating the origin of the leak

01:28:36.460 --> 01:28:40.140
while the scientific community works to
verify and replicate the findings.

01:28:40.380 --> 01:28:43.340
Doctors are describing the development
as revolutionary.

01:28:44.460 --> 01:28:48.700
With the potential to save millions of
lives if confirmed and distributed

01:28:48.700 --> 01:28:53.580
safely, scientists across the globe are
already hailing the discovery. The

01:28:53.580 --> 01:28:57.980
source of the leak remains unknown, but
early analysis suggests the data is

01:28:57.980 --> 01:28:58.980
credible.

01:29:04.220 --> 01:29:06.840
Tell me about the mountains.

01:29:12.440 --> 01:29:13.860
Like being on top of the world.
